# Better Auth + Auth Security (Archestimator)

Better Auth 1.6.23 is wired against D1. Mounted at `/api/auth/[...all]`. Google OAuth + magic link. **D1-backed, not Postgres.**

## Auth Architecture

- **Better Auth handler**: `src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`
- **Route gate proxy**: `src/lib/auth/request-proxy.ts` — exported via `src/middleware.ts`
- **D1 stores**: `account-actions`, `account-settings`, `account-audit` (see `src/lib/auth/*-d1-store.ts`)
- **Closed beta**: `src/lib/auth/closed-beta-d1-store.ts`
- **Dev auth**: `src/lib/auth/dev-auth.ts`

## Authorization Layers (Defense In Depth)

D1 has no RLS. Authorization enforced at:

1. **Better Auth route gate** (`src/lib/auth/request-proxy.ts`) — first-line route protection
2. **Repository helpers** — every read/write takes authz context (see `11-cloudflare-d1-repositories.mdc`)
3. **Server Actions** — re-validate session + ownership before every mutation
4. **Rate limiting** — DB-durable via `security_rate_limit_events` table

Fail-closed by default. If any check is missing or ambiguous, deny.

## Credential Material Handling

Distinct materials with distinct visibility rules — never collapse:

| Material | Storage | Visibility | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| Raw bearer token (invite, share) | SHA-256 hash in D1; raw only at issuance/acceptance | URL-carried, single-use | One-time acceptance flow |
| Password hash (publication) | bcrypt/argon2 in D1 | Never client-visible | Publication password unlock |
| Session cookie | Better Auth managed | Client cookie, httpOnly, Secure | Persistent session |
| OAuth state | Ephemeral | Short-lived | CSRF protection during OAuth |
| Magic link token | Hashed in D1 + TTL | URL-carried | Time-bounded login |
| Password reset / unlock | Hashed in D1 + TTL | URL-carried | Recovery flow |

**Rule**: If a public route requires a raw bearer value, a stored hash is NOT a substitute. If a Server Action must recover raw material, it must authorize first and keep recovery server-only.

## Invite + Share Token Flow

- `collaboration_invitations` table: hashed tokens, expiry, role, workspace/project scope
- `project_publications` table: hashed tokens, optional password hashes, recipient list
- Acceptance path: `/invite/[token]/` (auth required) -> accept -> invalidate token
- Public share path: `/share/[token]/` (no auth required) -> optional password gate -> render snapshot

Read `src/lib/collaboration/invites/` and `src/lib/publication/` for the actual patterns.

## Rate Limiting (DB-Durable)

`security_rate_limit_events` table provides persistent rate limiting across:

- Publication / share endpoints (P10 lockout threshold)
- AI surfaces (when enabled)
- Invite entry paths
- Export paths

App-layer enforcement, not Cloudflare WAF. Read `src/lib/observability/` and existing rate-limit helpers before adding new ones.

## Server Action Auth Checklist

Every Server Action that mutates:

- [ ] Better Auth session via `src/lib/auth/`
- [ ] Workspace membership check
- [ ] Role check (owner/admin/editor/viewer)
- [ ] Resource ownership check
- [ ] Input schema validation (Zod or repo schema)
- [ ] Rate limit check (if on a sensitive surface)
- [ ] Idempotency safe (retry doesn't duplicate)
- [ ] Audit event written (where applicable)

## Forbidden

- Storing raw tokens in D1 (always hash first)
- Logging raw tokens, hashes, cookies, or session IDs
- Passing auth context through client props — re-derive on server
- Trusting client-supplied `userId` or `workspaceId`
- Skipping authz because "the UI hides it"
- `as any` to bypass session typing — fix the types
- Long-lived tokens without explicit expiry + revocation path

## Audit Trail

Auth/permission/account events write to:

- `account_security_events` — auth actions, password changes, OAuth links
- `collaboration_audit_events` — workspace/invite/share mutations
- `estimate_sheet_events` — estimate mutation history

Use the existing audit helpers; don't write raw INSERTs.

## Closed Beta (If Active)

`src/lib/auth/closed-beta-d1-store.ts` gates registration behind an allow-list. Check `closedBeta` field on auth flows. Disabled by default unless env-flagged.

## Dev Auth

`src/lib/auth/dev-auth.ts` provides dev-only shortcuts. **Never import in production code paths.** Gated by `NODE_ENV === "development"`.
